message: "A manuscript describing this resource will be submitted soon. Until it is published, please cite this website as below, with the version and your access date; once the manuscript is available, please cite the manuscript. Also cite the underlying studies listed on each study page."
title: "717 Atlas: a haplotype-resolved gene atlas for Populus tremula x alba clone INRA 717-1B4"
abstract: >-
  A static, browsable atlas of the 63,960 gene models in the two phased haplotypes of hybrid
  poplar clone 717, integrating GENESPACE synteny across a 12-genome panel, genEra
  phylostratigraphy, Phytozome v5.1 functional annotation, HAP1/HAP2 syntelog pairs with Ka/Ks,
  and a 652-sample RNA-seq expression atlas drawn from 28 curated studies. Duplication classes,
  whole-genome duplication anchor pairs, cross-haplotype relationship categories and tissue
  specificity are those of the accompanying dissertation, and its master tables are offered for
  download. It adds tandem-array and paralog duplication context (inferred calls), predicted
  protein disorder and ESMFold-derived secondary structure, peptide matches from a re-search of
  five public Populus mass-spectrometry datasets (several from other Populus species, mostly on
  shared peptides), 46,141 reciprocal one-to-one orthologs to Populus trichocarpa from the same
  synteny run, Ka/Ks against P. trichocarpa for 52,232 genes, and accessible-chromatin and
  histone-mark calls from GEO GSE128434 measured in P. trichocarpa and shown on each gene's
  ortholog, not measured on 717. The lineage-specific candidates (phylostratum 18 or above;
  776 HAP1, 835 HAP2) are from the genEra rerun that added Idesia polycarpa and searched the full
  comparison panel; the final lineage-specific gene set is 583 HAP1 and 621 HAP2 genes.
